  nonce: 6a9a  # 6a9a
  message: "PR #47 (dev a26410666a): fixed. Read-write @property (getter + @x.setter/@x.deleter) now resolves the READ. Root cause: getter+setter share qualified name C.x; the name-keyed registries (symbol_by_name, the (path,qualified) index) are last-write-wins so they retain the setter, whose decorator is the dotted 'x.setter', failing _resolve_property_getter's bare-'property' gate. Fix: _build_property_getter_index builds a (path,qualified_name)->getter map from the PRE-collapse per-file symbols, wired into both the full-pipeline main loop and the single-file extract_nodes path + threaded through _extract_edges; _resolve_property_getter consults it first. Behavioral evidence: TestReadWritePropertyResolves.test_read_write_property_getter_resolves + test_getter_setter_deleter_property_read_resolves (production path via extract_nodes) — c.val read emits its receiver_type_hint='C' read edge (before: 0 edges); + 2 unit tests (dedicated-index-beats-setter, present-but-empty fall-through). Full affected slice green, 100% cov. NOTE: cached_property is a separate decorator (not @property), out of scope/unchanged."  # 6a9a
